.claude/settings.local.json
# `.claude/rules/` holds workspace refresh artifacts (written by
# `macf rules refresh`), not source. Canonical rule files live at
# `plugin/rules/`. Without this ignore, the refresh-produced copy
# appears as a persistent untracked file and causes `macf self-update`
# to refuse with a dirty-tree error. Both agents hit this same day
# — see `project_untracked_coordination_artifact.md`.
.claude/rules/

# `.claude/scripts/*.sh` are MANAGED (DR-029 amendment, macf#598): tool-written
# copies of `packages/macf/plugin/scripts/` + `packages/macf/scripts/`,
# installed by `macf update` / `rules refresh`. Tracking installed output
# creates a second writer alongside the tool — `git checkout`/`reset` and
# `macf update` disagree, and nothing arbitrates; a `reset --hard` silently
# reinstalled two-month-stale hooks THREE TIMES in one day and blocked every
# `gh` call each time (groundnuty/macf#1392). The design surface stays
# `plugin/scripts/` (+ `packages/macf/scripts/`) — reviewed, tracked, source.
# `macf-statusline.sh` has no canonical source (hand-authored, workspace-only
# statusline customization — operator-preserved per the same taxonomy) and
# stays tracked despite living in this directory; the negation below is
# belt-and-suspenders since an already-tracked file isn't affected by a
# later-added ignore rule.
.claude/scripts/*
!.claude/scripts/macf-statusline.sh
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.env
.env.local
coverage/
.worktrees/
*.pem

# Local CLI/gh state dirs (e.g. packages/*/.local/state/gh/) — never source
.local/

# Local subagent worktrees (never committed)
.claude/worktrees/

# MACF runtime dirs (per-workspace env files, certs, registry, channel-server
# runtime state) generated by `macf init`/`update` — never source. Matches
# `.macf/` at the root and `.claude/.macf/` (any depth). The channel-server
# log cluster itself now lives in the agent HOME (macf#642); this backstops
# the workspace runtime dir from ever being committed.
.macf/
